        "ids": [
          {
            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "2506771"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in the cluster-proxy service-proxy component used in Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management for Kubernetes (RHACM) and multicluster-engine (MCE). The service-proxy appends impersonation group headers to proxied requests without first removing caller-supplied values, and the spoke ServiceAccount holds unrestricted impersonation permissions. An authenticated hub principal can inject an Impersonate-Group header to escalate to cluster-admin on every managed cluster.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "cluster-proxy: cluster-proxy: Impersonation header injection in service-proxy grants cluster-admin on every managed cluster",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "A flaw was found in the cluster-proxy service-proxy component of Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management for Kubernetes and multicluster-engine that allows an authenticated hub principal to escalate privileges to cluster-admin across all managed clusters. This is due to improper handling of impersonation group headers, enabling unauthorized administrative access. While the impact of successful exploitation is severe, the attack requires authenticated access to the ACM hub cluster, which is a management-plane component not typically exposed to untrusted networks. Exploitation also depends on knowledge of the cluster-proxy architecture and deliberate construction of requests targeting specific managed clusters. These prerequisites significantly reduce the likelihood of opportunistic or widespread exploitation.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
        ],
